WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Sunlight streams through the
air and warms the ground.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.050
The warm ground then sends
energy back out, towards space.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.810
But not all of that energy makes it.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.990
Some is held back on the way out,

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.670
and the air near the ground
stays warmer than it would

6
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.150
otherwise be.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.910
Sunlight got in easily,

8
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.590
so why can't all the energy
get back out as easily?

9
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.870
In this mission, you'll follow
energy from the Sun to the

10
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.490
Earth, and back out again.

11
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.570
You'll meet the greenhouse gases,

12
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.050
see what they do to
the outgoing energy,

13
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.150
and compare the natural
greenhouse effect with the extra

14
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.470
warming that comes from
adding more of these gases.

15
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.450
Your mission: explain what stops
some energy escaping to space.
